{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01N8nujRQnTeefY5NS9rihm6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (plain markdown files as the source of truth, Python stdlib only).\n\n**Core purpose & what it does:**\n- A **GTD-style task/project manager** built on markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, domain files under `domains/`) that walks tasks through a lifecycle: Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, each with optional notes.\n- Ships as a **persistent local web app** (`anchor_gui.py`) â€” a self-contained stdlib HTTP server bound to `http://localhost:8777`, run as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. It generates the full dashboard HTML on every request and writes changes straight back to the markdown.\n- Includes a **CLI engine** (`anchor.py`) that mirrors the same logic (done/add/capture/cancel/save/restore) and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n- Has a **daily self-test** (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) that runs at 5 AM via Task Scheduler, exercising every endpoint and the R&D surfaces (all model calls stubbed), and writes dated reports to `health_reports/`.\n\n**The major built-out subsystem â€” the R&D \"Project Cockpit\":**\n- An **R&D control surface** (evolved through v2 â†’ v3 â†’ v4, all merged to master) that turns each project's window into a mission-control cockpit for \"trio\" work: the research â†’ planning â†’ build skill pipeline (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman).\n- It ships **real interactive ConPTY terminals** (the one declared native-dependency exception, `pywinpty`, used lazily in `pty_manager.py` only), **per-session git-worktree isolation**, a **session registry**, **cached/validated AI-generated summaries**, **per-lane doc roles**, a **cost/tokens/time rollup**, a **grass-catcher idea board**, and **type-aware deliverable launch** (skill/tool/service/program/doc).\n- The current v4/v4.1 UI is the **Paradigm-2 cockpit**: each lane is a tile with one honest status light (green/amber/red/grey); clicking expands an **inline panel in place** with a summary on top and a resizable xterm.js terminal below; new sessions auto-load the lane's skill **once** and greet once (fixing the old repeating-prompt bug).\n- Branded as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢.\"\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: this summary is drawn from the project's `CLAUDE.md` and memory index rather than from re-reading the source this turn. If you want, I can verify any specific claim (e.g., that the v4 cockpit is actually wired up as described) against the live code."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45832,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93cef30b-2df2-4366-830b-ab260c5a3f74","uuid":"73e9b6bd-0cd9-4d8d-a65b-9e44030e4ecc","request_id":"req_011Cc2LKv91edvKN8kYhB9th"}
